                "location": "engine/review/app/evidence.go:90-96",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "CheckEvidence now refuses a review-report whose stored verdict does not parse against its result. This is a deliberate, tested tightening: a record that previously passed (verdict file with matching digest but unparseable or naming an unknown finding id) is now refused with exit 1. Failure path is covered by app and cmd tests, but the success path with a valid verdict relies on existing tests; no new test pins that a verdict parsed against the result's parsed reply (not a different object) is accepted when the result has multiple findings.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/review/app/evidence.go:90-96",
                  "engine/review/app/evidence_test.go:305-328",
                  "engine/cmd/roles_evidence_test.go:271-282"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 15 manifest paths. The only behavioral change is in engine/review/app/evidence.go: the verifier-report evidence is now additionally held to reviewverdict.Parse against the parsed result, wrapped as an EvidenceError with kind and ref. Tests added at the app level (unparseable bytes, unknown finding id) and at the cmd level (non-verdict file with matching digest) assert the sentinel and the named kind/ref, so the new failure paths are proved at the cheapest level.",
              "The cmd-level test TestRunHandsRolesAppendTheDepsItWasHanded proves the evidence check uses the deps' working directory, covering both refusal (no repository, nothing stored) and storage paths.",
              "The check_exempt_test addition covers the CheckOneCommit refusal for a stored exemption whose base is not the head's first parent, with the file named in the error.",
              "Remaining changes are doc/test restructuring (grouped fragments, shared requireHelpFacts helper), comments, README and CHANGELOG wording; the docs tests still assert the same facts and now name the rule on failure. No regression found in them.",
              "The README table edit narrows rows to match Check behavior as already documented (a blocking result wins over exemption), not a code change."
            ]
          }
